.TH ISOFORGE 1 "2026-09-03" "isoforge 2.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
isoforge \- downloads Linux images, writes them to USB (single image or Ventoy multi-ISO), and builds custom installable ISOs from a recipe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B isoforge
[OPTIONS] [COMMAND [COMMAND_OPTIONS]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Isoforge downloads Linux images, writes them to USB (single image or Ventoy multi-ISO), and builds custom installable ISOs from a recipe.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B download
Download one or more ISOs from config.json. Options: --config PATH, -h, --help.
.TP
.B burn
Write an ISO from download_dir, or a browsed local ISO, to a drive. Options: --config PATH, -h, --help.
.TP
.B build
Build a custom installable ISO from a recipe. Options: -r/--recipe PATH, -o/--output DIR, --config PATH, --work-dir DIR, --dry-run, --smoke-test, --keep, --version, -h/--help.
.TP
.B setup
Install project dependencies. Parameters: PACKAGE. Options: -h, --help.
.TP
.B help [COMMAND]
Show top-level help or command help for download, burn, build, or setup.
.TP
.B --config PATH
Override config file path for the TUI flow.
.TP
.B --version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/isoforge/config.json
Default configuration when installed system-wide.
.TP
.I $HOME/Downloads/iso_images
Default download directory used when the \fBdownload_dir\fR configuration option is missing or empty.
